    "result_text": "The build is green. The `AcceptanceTest` is the only test in the project, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes owner creation/retrieval expose a `displayName` formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. Since DTOs are generated from this spec by the openapi-generator plugin, `OwnerDto` now carries the field (and it stays absent from `OwnerFields`, so it's response-only).\n\n**2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped it in the DTO conversion, keeping the formatting where DTO shaping belongs:\n\n```java\n@Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(formatDisplayName(owner))\")\nOwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n\ndefault String formatDisplayName(Owner owner) {\n    return owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName();\n}\n```\n\nThe presentation format lives in the mapper (a single small method), the domain `Owner` entity is untouched, and the read-only field flows through every existing `toOwnerDto` call (create response, `GET`, list) without duplicating logic.",
